```
later, we refactored the interface to look like this:
```hcl
variable "descheduler" {
  description = "The configuration for `descheduler` addon"
  type = object({
    enabled      = optional(bool, true)
    force_update = optional(bool, false)
    policies = optional(map(object({
      schedule                           = optional(string, "*/10 * * * *")
      nodeSelector                       = optional(string, "role=node")
      topology_spread_constraint_enabled = optional(bool, false)
      utilizationThresholds = optional(
        object({
          cpu          = number
          memory       = number
          cpuTarget    = number
          memoryTarget = number
        }),
        {
          cpu          = 50
          memory       = 50
          cpuTarget    = 90
          memoryTarget = 90
        }
      )
      })), {
      default = {}
    })
  })
  default = {}
}
```
`topology_spread_constraint_enabled` and `utilizationThresholds` were removed, while `policies` was added.
separately, a different member of the team upgraded the module from a version with the first interface, to a version with the second interface. call parameters were not changed, and we did not inspect the resulting plan closely. we ended up applying the changes.
we would have preferred getting a plan error, and being forced to update the call site for this variable, but additional object keys are not an error. they are silently discarded during type conversion:
https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/expressions/type-constraints#:~:text=Values%20with%20additional%20keys%20can%20still%20match%20an%20object%20type%2C%20but%20the%20extra%20attributes%20are%20discarded%20during%20type%20conversion.
